     "level": 5,
     "name": "Pushed Too Far",
     "type": "",
     "flavor": "When you press beyond reason and find yourself surrounded, you don't retreat—you force space.",
     "cost": "",
     "description": "**Bullhead Charge**\nCost: 1 AP | 1 BP\nYou lower your head and drive forward, attempting to smash through the creature blocking your escape. Make a competing Brawn Check against the targeted creature. If you are at or below half HP, you gain Small Advantage on this check.\n- On a success: You force your way past the creature, knocking them Prone, and immediately disengage from them. This movement does not provoke Opportunity Attacks from the targeted creature.\n- On a failure: You fail to break through their space. The creature gains Small Disadvantage on their next attack made against you.\n\n**In Too Deep**\nCost: 1 AP | 1 BP\nYou attempt to escape by vaulting over, climbing onto, or bounding across the creatures surrounding you. The maximum number of creatures you can jump over is equal to your Traversal Modifier + 1, to a minimum of 1, compared against the Horde Density of the creatures you are attempting to cross.\n\nHorde Density Values:\n| Size Category | Distance Modifier |\n|---|---|\n| Puny | 1 |\n| Small | 1 |\n| Medium | 2 |\n| Large | 2 |\n| Massive | 3 |\n| Gargantuan | 4 |\n| Colossal | 5 |\n\nIf your allowed number of creatures meets or exceeds the required Horde Density, you successfully escape the horde without provoking disengage-based reactions from those creatures.\n\n**Making Space**\n1 AP | 1 BP\nYou swing, shove, and bash outward, forcing the creatures around you to give ground.\nWhen you take this Bonus Action, all creatures adjacent to you are pushed 5 feet directly away from you. Creatures smaller than you are pushed 10 feet instead. To successfully push the horde back, you must make a successful Attack Roll against the horde's Resistance Value.\n\nHorde Resistance Values:\n| Size Category | Horde Resistance Modifier |\n|---|---|\n| Puny | 0 |\n| Small | 0 |\n| Medium | 1 |\n| Large | 2 |\n| Massive | 3 |\n| Gargantuan | 5 |\n| Colossal | 5 |\n\nOn a success, the affected creatures are pushed as described. On a failure, no movement occurs.",
