      {
       "augId": "cls-templar-aug-nox",
       "name": "Avatar of Judgment",
       "type": "Passive",
       "tagline": "",
       "cost": "Passive",
       "appearance": "The Lock shatters completely.\nYou are no longer yourself.\nA fully fractured, blazing golden halo spins above your head, crackling with divine energy. Massive curved golden horns crown your skull. Your body is encased in interlocking shards of black and radiant gold crystal, your former armor entirely consumed and reforged into living divine plating. Your posture is permanently hunched, predatory and inevitable. Your hands are fully clawed, elongated into instruments of execution. Your feet end in taloned digits that scar the ground with radiant fractures wherever you stand. Your eyes burn like twin suns without warmth. You are the Avatar of Judgment.",
       "description": "While your Lock is Open:\n- Your form fully transforms into the Avatar of Nox temporarily.\n- Your weapon attacks deal plus 10 Divine Damage.\n- Your Divine Damage ignores RES and IMM.\n\n**Judgment Absolute**\n- Once per turn, when you deal Divine Damage to a creature, you may declare it Condemned.\n- A Condemned creature become easier to hit reducing their effective AC by 2.\n- If the creature is Evil, it instead takes double that amount.\n\n**Execution Decree**\n- If a creature is reduced below 25 percent Health by your Divine Damage, you may immediately make one additional weapon attack against it without spending AP.\n- This may occur once per turn.\n\nWhile Avatar of Judgment is active:\n- You gain plus 2 AC and plus 4 EC.\n- You are immune to Fear.\n- Your presence counts as both Divine and Overwhelming for all effects.\n\nWhen your Lock closes:\n- You suffer 1 level of fatigue.",
       "flaw": "",
       "quote": ""
      }
