     "name": "Consume Burden",
     "type": "",
     "flavor": "",
     "cost": "",
     "description": "You learn the sacred act of suffering in place of another.\nYou gain the spell:\n\n**Consume Burden**\nReaction | Sight | Verbal\nCost: 1 RP | PP varies\nRange: Presence\nWhen an allied creature within Presence gains a burden (debuff, curse, condition, or harmful effect), you may transfer that burden to yourself. The burden functions exactly as written when applied to you.\n\nBurden Restriction\n- Consume Burden may only transfer Mundane burdens.\n- You cannot transfer: Advanced burdens; Legendary burdens; Ascended burdens\n\nScripture Learning\nIf you consume a burden you have never carried before:\n- You may only consume that specific burden once per day until it is learned.\nDuring any rest (SR, Light, or Heavy), you may record that burden into your Scripture.\nOnce recorded:\n- That burden is permanently learned and scribed.\n- It may be consumed freely in the future also long as you have your scribes.\nIf a burden has multiple stages, each stage must be learned individually.",
