   "category": "Items",
   "summary": "The families of weapons and how they play.",
   "text": "| Group | Description |\n|---|---|\n| Light Weapons | Fast, low AP, rely on crits/talents for impact. |\n| One-Handed Versatile Weapons | Mid AP, mid damage, flexible talents. |\n| Polearms & Reach Weapons | Longer reach, situational control, higher AP variants hit hard. |\n| Heavy Two-Handed Weapons | High AP, high BD, battlefield control and stance breakers. |\n| Exotic / Special Weapons | Niche, bleed, AoE, and trick-weapons. |\n| Ranged Weapons | AP scales with size; crit bonuses sometimes swingier than melee. |\n| Harmony Weapons | Forged in pursuit of balance between body, spirit, and steel, Harmony weapons embody the ideals of precision and flow. |\n| Solar Weapons | Forged in devotion to the sun and the divine order, Solar Weapons embody the might of pharaohs and the blessing of the gods. Their designs combine brutal practicality with sacred symbolism |",
